 <name>beacon</name>
 <channel>pecl.php.net</channel>
 <summary>PHP-FPM state beacon and governance scheduling substrate</summary>
 <description>beacon is a PHP-FPM C extension that solves the tension between FPM's short-lived worker processes and the long-lived state required for service governance. It does three things FPM cannot: perception (self-counting pool-level health), scheduling (spawning a persistent governance worker), and caching (double-buffered shm for zero-I/O node reads).</description>
